new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ddb1e47
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# pastebin
+
+A loopback-only HTTP service for sharing text snippets. Create a paste by POSTing
+JSON, read it back as structured data or as plain text, and revoke it with a secret
+issued at creation. Pastes may carry a lifetime and survive restarts.
+
+Python 3.11+, **no runtime dependencies** — standard library only.
+
+## Run it
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m pastebin serve --port 8080 --data ./pastes-data
+```
+
+The data directory is created if absent (parents included, mode `0700`), and stdout
+carries exactly one line:
+
+```text
+listening on 127.0.0.1:8080
+```
+
+Use `--port 0` to let the kernel pick a free port — the line reports the port
+actually bound. The bind address is always `127.0.0.1`; there is deliberately no
+`--host` flag. Any startup failure prints to stderr, exits non-zero, and prints no
+readiness line. `Ctrl-C` stops the service and exits `0`.
+
+Full argument, exit-status, and failure-message contract:
+[`specs/001-pastebin-service/contracts/cli.md`](specs/001-pastebin-service/contracts/cli.md).
+
+## Routes
+
+| Method | Path | Operation | Success |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `POST` | `/pastes` | Create a paste | `201` |
+| `GET` | `/pastes/<id>` | Read metadata and content | `200` |
+| `GET` | `/pastes/<id>/raw` | Read the content as plain text | `200` |
+| `DELETE` | `/pastes/<id>` | Revoke, via the `X-Delete-Token` header | `204` |
+
+Every other request — unknown path, unsupported method on a known path, unknown
+sub-resource, trailing slash — is `404`. There is no `405` and no `Allow` header.
+Errors are always JSON: `{"error": "<message>"}`.
+
+```bash
+curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/pastes -d '{"content": "hello", "expires_in": 3600}'
+# {"id": "...", "delete_token": "...", "url": "/pastes/..."}
+
+curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/pastes/$ID        # {"id", "content", "created_at", "expires_at"}
+curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/pastes/$ID/raw    # hello
+curl -s -X DELETE -H "X-Delete-Token: $TOKEN" http://127.0.0.1:8080/pastes/$ID
+```
+
+`content` is required, must be a string, and may not exceed 65 536 UTF-8 bytes
+(`413` if it does). `expires_in` is optional and must be a whole number of seconds
+from 1 to 2 592 000; absent means the paste never expires. Other fields are ignored.
+The `delete_token` is returned exactly once, in the `201` — no read ever discloses it.
+
+Full request and response contract, including every error message and the precedence
+rules between statuses:
+[`specs/001-pastebin-service/contracts/http-api.md`](specs/001-pastebin-service/contracts/http-api.md).
+
+## Tests
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src pytest -q
+```
+
+The suite must pass with zero failures, skips, and `xfail`s. It drives a real server
+over real HTTP and runs `python -m pastebin` as a subprocess for the startup cases;
+like the runtime, it uses only the standard library plus `pytest`.
+
+`tests/test_requirement_coverage.py` is the gate that keeps the requirement-to-test
+mapping honest: it fails if any requirement id (`FR-001` … `FR-029`, `SR-001` …
+`SR-012`) is referenced by no test name or docstring.
+
+## Layout
+
+```text
+src/pastebin/
+├── __main__.py   # python -m pastebin → cli.main()
+├── cli.py        # arguments, data-directory setup, bind, readiness line, exit codes
+├── server.py     # ThreadingHTTPServer + handler: routing, framing, errors
+├── store.py      # PasteStore: atomic writes, path containment, revocation
+└── models.py     # record shape, validation rules, timestamps, id generation
+```
+
+Design documents live under `specs/001-pastebin-service/`: the specification, the
+plan and its research decisions, the data model, the two contracts above, and a
+runnable `quickstart.md`.
+
+## Storage and security notes
+
+Each paste is one UTF-8 JSON record at `<data_dir>/<id>.json`, written to an
+`O_EXCL` temporary file with mode `0600` set at creation, `fsync`ed, then moved into
+place with `os.replace` — so a concurrent reader sees the complete record or none of
+it, and the file is never momentarily readable by other users. The directory is
+`0700`.
+
+Identifiers (22 chars, 128 bits) and revocation secrets (43 chars, 256 bits) come
+from `secrets`; the secret is compared with `hmac.compare_digest` inside the same
+lock as the removal. An identifier from a request is matched against
+`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}` before it is joined to a path, and the resolved path is confirmed
+to lie inside the data directory. Expiry is computed per request against the current
+clock — there is no sweeper and no startup scan. Nothing the service returns contains
+a revocation secret, a filesystem path, or a stack trace.
